[prb@chinet.chi.il.us (Paul Botts) writes:]
[] Well, so he's right - there is no (or virtually no) effective difference
[] between strength of 18/01 and 18/50 and 25. Why not? If this is the
[] case, why bother with the higher strength numbers at all? And why
[] shouldn't people who have died after wishing for gloves of power
[] (instead of something actually useful) be extraordinarily ticked off?

assuming HARD, and if wishing for individual pieces of armor is to
be considered a wise thing then wishing for:
blessed +3 gauntlets of dexterity

is better than wishing for gauntlets of power.

in play-testing, i've found that MAXCARRCAP equal to 200 as opposed to
120 under HARD works better.  along with this, i use adjusted carrying
capacity and damage bonus equations, etc.  the carrying capacity stuff
uses (5 * ulevel) and adds (5 * str) for strengths below 18/01, adds 90
plus ((fractional strength + 1) / 2) for strengths between 18/01 and
18/** (a max bonus of 140) and adds 170 for gauntlets of power (all
adjusted to a limit of MAXCARRCAP, of course).  this gives strength
increases a consistent effect (amongst other things).

in all this, i have faith that dev team will devise a better scheme
for these things ...

